<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
<h1>Honda Click vs Yamaha Mio: A Selection Guide for Hanoi Scooter Rental</h1>
<p>The Click and the Mio are the entry tier's two headline automatics, and they are closer to each other than any other pair in the catalogue. Same tier, same 150,000 VND daily rate, same city-purpose character. Choosing between them is less a strategic decision and more a fitting: the right one is whichever machine disappears under you on a slow loop of the block.</p>
<p>This guide compares them honestly: how each feels in Hanoi conditions, the small differences in comfort and storage, pricing, and which riders each suits. Start with the <a href="/hanoi-scooter-rental/">Hanoi scooter rental</a> hub, frame the budget with the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> guide, and read <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental in Hanoi</a> for long stays. The long-standing <a href="/hanoi-scooter-rental/honda-click-vs-yamaha-mio-hanoi/">Click versus Mio comparison</a> carries the model-by-model detail.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">Two machines, one tier</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">How they feel in Hanoi traffic</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">Comfort and storage differences</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">Verified rental prices</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-5">Riders who suit the Click</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-6">Riders who suit the Mio</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-7">Inspecting and test sitting</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-8">Making the final call</a></li>
